  "semanticFindings": [
    "Public percent_encode Iterator<Item=&str> and AsciiSet const remove operate with defaults disabled. Uppercase percent-byte table and non-ASCII refusal membership are verified in pinned cached upstream source.",
    "Helper strictly decodes raw units via std::char::decode_utf16, uses char.encode_utf8 on [u8;4], consumes public iterator chunks into sole output Vec<u16>. No String temporary or custom manual surrogate/UTF8/hex scanner remains in production.",
    "Nine -_.!~*'() punctuation characters plus ASCII alphanumeric remain unescaped; space is %20, percent/slash/reserved/control bytes escape uppercase; BMP/astral boundaries match defining behavior.",
    "Owner local U16/error mappings remain exact URIError, URI malformed, with code None where defined. Every caller/type/quote/public body and maintained original test outside the three encoder functions is byte-identical.",
    "Rows every-slot raw scope remains copied raw, as originally defined. Receipt empty-component and linkage nonempty/cohort validation precede URI decoding. Distinct owner value/error profiles remain local.",
    "New retained helper tests are literal cases and malformed vectors; no copied old production scanner or counting allocator is retained in product tests. Private original scanner oracle is qualification-only."
  ],
